{"language_code":"eng","language_probability":0.947242796421051,"text":"Your dream bag is the one everybody recognizes on sight, and that's the problem. So here are five bags you should buy instead. Number five, Bottega Veneta. No logo anywhere, the weave does the talking, and only the right people can read it from across the room. Number four, the Margaux from The Row. Soft leather, that same shape, none of the hardware, and the insiders wait for this one. Number three, Valextra, Milan nineteen thirty-seven. Clean lines, nothing loud, and the Easy Day has been the house icon since twenty eleven. Number two, Delvaux, Brussels eighteen twenty-nine. It calls itself the oldest fine leather house in the world, and you can walk in on a Tuesday and leave with its best bag. And number one, a brand almost nobody has heard of yet, and the one I pre-ordered. This is the Vivienne from Valentra. Vegetable tanned leather all the way through, a belted brass turn lock, braided leather trim, and no logo anywhere. It's soft, so it slouches and molds to you as you carry it. It comes in four colors. It's twenty-five percent off on pre-order right now, one forty-nine instead of one ninety-nine, and the first run ships in October. I left the link below.","words":[{"text":"Your","start":0.079,"end":0.199,"type":"word","logprob":-1.7881377516459906e-6},{"text":" ","start":0.199,"end":0.299,"type":"spacing","logprob":-2.3841855067985307e-7},{"text":"dream","start":0.299,"end":0.519,"type":"word","logprob":-2.3841855067985307e-7},{"text":" ","start":0.519,"end":0.579,"type":"spacing","logprob":-1.7881377516459906e-6},{"text":"bag","start":0.579,"end":0.939,"type":"word","logprob":-1.7881377516459906e-6},{"text":" ","start":0.939,"end":0.979,"type":"spacing","logprob":-1.1920928244535389e-7},{"text":"is","start":0.979,"end":1.059,"type":"word","logprob":-1.1920928244535389e-7},{"text":" ","start":1.059,"end":1.119,"type":"spacing","logprob":-1.1920928244535389e-7},{"text":"the","start":1.12,